Diagram requirements (use Mermaid or Markmap code blocks; choose the diagram style according to paper archetype and module needs):
- If a diagram is inferred rather than explicitly shown in the paper, prefix its title with `[Inferred]`.
- Mermaid syntax rule: node IDs must stay simple ASCII alphanumerics such as `NodeA` or `step1`. Put complex wording in labels, for example `NodeA["Complex description"]`.
- Diagrams support the text; they must not replace the text. Always explain the diagram after the code block.
- Module B must include a full-paper Markmap outline, even if the paper does not provide an explicit outline.
- Survey papers must include a taxonomy plus representative-work diagram (`flowchart TD`).
- Method papers must include a process diagram (`flowchart TD`) and a data-flow diagram (`flowchart LR`).
- System papers must include an architecture diagram (`flowchart LR`) and a data-flow diagram (`flowchart LR`).
- Module C3 should include a process diagram (`flowchart TD`) when the paper is method-oriented.
- Module D should include an architecture diagram (`flowchart LR`) when the paper is system-oriented.
- Modules C4 and C5 may include data-flow or protocol relationship diagrams (`flowchart LR`) when useful.
- Module E may include a performance/trade-off diagram (`flowchart TD`) when useful.
- Module H may include an experiment-setup or benchmark-coverage diagram (`flowchart TD`) when useful.

Reference examples (follow the code-fence format and keep node IDs simple):
